      "rev_n_1_35be70_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_35be70_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_35be70",
        "thought_text": "The current approach is correct in its dynamic programming formulation, but it's not accurately counting the number of good plans. The issue lies in how the total number of bugs is calculated and compared to the limit. We need to modify the calculation of total bugs for each plan to ensure we're considering all possible distributions of lines among programmers.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_35be70_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_05716b2fad",
        "created_at": 1794537115.392375
      },
      "rev_n_2_b2f435_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_b2f435_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_b2f435",
        "thought_text": "Instead of using a 3D DP table, consider using a 2D DP table with rolling arrays to optimize space complexity and potentially improve time efficiency.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_b2f435_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_0703378875",
        "created_at": 1794537143.8428135
      },
      "rev_n_3_ca0b15_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_ca0b15_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_ca0b15",
        "thought_text": "The current approach using recursion with memoization is inefficient for large inputs due to the exponential nature of exploring all possible plans. Instead, we can use dynamic programming with a 3D table to optimize the solution. This approach will significantly reduce the time complexity and avoid the Time Limit Exceeded (TLE) error.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_ca0b15_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_a8caa5d822",
        "created_at": 1794537178.2838879
      },
