      "rev_n_7_c09b98_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_c09b98_1",
        "node_id": "n_7_c09b98",
        "thought_text": "The error in the current implementation is likely due to an incorrect state transition logic. The current approach is considering all possible combinations of lines for each programmer, which leads to overcounting. Instead, we should consider the contribution of each programmer to the total number of lines and bugs, and update the DP table accordingly. This approach will ensure that we count each valid plan exactly once.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "85810810917386540",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_7_c09b98_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_87d8deb0c3",
        "created_at": 1794537298.3105783
      },
      "rev_n_10_07fbc5_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_07fbc5_0",
        "node_id": "n_10_07fbc5",
        "thought_text": "Switch to a bottom-up dynamic programming approach to avoid recursion and stack overflow issues.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2483145616480252800",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794537315.47768
      },
      "rev_n_11_202a63_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_11_202a63_0",
        "node_id": "n_11_202a63",
        "thought_text": "Use a 3D DP table where dp[i][j][k] represents the number of ways to distribute j lines among i programmers with a total of k bugs.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2483145616480252800",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794537315.4776974
      },
      "rev_n_12_63236b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_12_63236b_0",
        "node_id": "n_12_63236b",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through programmers, lines, and bug counts to fill the DP table, considering all possible ways to distribute lines and accumulate bugs.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2483145616480252800",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794537315.4777055
      },
      "rev_n_11_202a63_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_11_202a63_1",
        "node_id": "n_11_202a63",
        "thought_text": "The current approach using a 3D DP table is correct in its logic, but there's a subtle error in the implementation. The issue lies in the initialization of the DP table. We need to initialize dp[0][0][0] = 1, but we should also initialize dp[i][0][0] = 1 for all i from 1 to n. This is because there's one way to distribute 0 lines among any number of programmers with 0 bugs. The current implementation is missing this initialization, which leads to incorrect results for some inputs.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2483145616480252800",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_11_202a63_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_3134a3aa65",
